-- A neural read whose input is a recursive walk (`lastOf`) over an observed
-- list: the list is in the query, so `lastOf zs` is a point and the read's
-- input is witnessed. main compiles generate only; probability and
-- integrate are silently absent. The non-recursive spellings
-- `readD (head (tail zs))` and `second zs = head (tail zs)` compile forward,
-- as do `lastOf zs < 0.0` (no neural read) and `main zs = readD (lastOf zs)`
-- (the list an argument). Idealized: p(([a, b], k)) = N(a) N(b) readD(b)[k].
-- Found by experiments_nest program-guided-diffusion (stage 2: reading the
-- perceiver at the clean end of a diffusion trajectory); docs task
-- neural-read-at-recursive-walk-of-observed-list-no-code.
expect-failure: no-code
